course: dictionary
lesson: 7065
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. To find out which meaning the writer means, read the sentence around the word. Patience is one of these words.
explain: The first meaning is about how you behave: being able to wait calmly, or keep trying, without getting angry or upset. In «Older dogs can learn new tricks with patience and treats», patience means you wait calmly and keep trying while the dog learns.
explain: The second meaning is a card game for one person. In the UK it is called patience; in the US it is called solitaire. To check which meaning fits, swap your meaning into the sentence. «Great discoveries are often stories of patience and luck» only makes sense with the first meaning, about waiting and trying.
fact: Patience means being able to wait calmly, or keep trying, without getting angry or upset.
fact: «Lose patience» and «run out of patience» mean you can no longer wait calmly.
fact: «Patience is a virtue» is a saying that means waiting calmly is a good quality to have.
fact: «Shy or frightened dogs make friends on their own terms; quiet patience works better than treats, calling or grabbing.»
fact: In the UK, patience is also the name of a card game for one person. In the US it is called solitaire.
exercise: Ravi keeps falling off his bike. His dad says, «Have patience, you will get it.» What does patience mean here? | *Being able to keep trying calmly | A card game for one person | Riding very fast | Giving up quickly
exercise: Dad's friend in the UK plays patience on his laptop, a card game for one person. What is this game called in the US? | Rummy | *Solitaire | Poker | Snap
exercise: «He tested my patience by asking the same question ten times.» What does «test someone's patience» mean? | *It makes someone find it hard to stay calm | It makes someone very happy | It makes someone want to play a card game | It makes someone fall asleep
test: «Shy or frightened dogs make friends on their own terms; quiet patience works better than treats, calling or grabbing.» What works better than treats, calling or grabbing? | *Quiet patience | Running fast | Loud shouting | Ignoring the dog
test: In «Older dogs can learn new tricks with patience and treats», what does patience mean? | Sleeping while the dog learns | A card game for one person | *Waiting calmly and keep trying | Being angry at the dog
exam: Which meaning of patience is used in «Patience is a virtue»? | *Waiting calmly, without getting angry | Being in a hurry to finish | A card game for one person | Losing a game on purpose
